--target=~/.config
# HAZARD: stow does NOT strip comments from this file. get_config_file_options()
# in bin/stow runs shellwords() over every line and pushes the result straight
# into the option list, so a word here that begins with a dash becomes a real
# option. A comment reading "the ignore flag is additive" once cost this file a
# silent, literal ignore rule for the word "is". Prose is fine; a leading dash
# anywhere in it is not. Verify any edit with:
#   stow -n -v --target=/tmp/somewhere .
#
# README.md, .gitignore and .gitmodules are NOT listed below: stow's built-in
# ignore list already skips them (plus LICENSE, .git, *~ and friends), and the
# ignore flag is additive rather than replacing, so repeating them did nothing.
# Trap: that built-in list only applies while the package has no
# .stow-local-ignore. Adding one REPLACES the built-in list wholesale, at which
# point .git, LICENSE, *~ etc. would suddenly start being stowed. If a
# .stow-local-ignore is ever introduced here, it must re-state those defaults.
#
# zsh, terminfo, herdr and macos are excluded here and installed by hand in
# install.common.sh / install.sh (different targets, or a real directory is
# required). There is no bin package: nothing needs to live in ~/.local/bin
# anymore — gitlab.com auth for `go get` is ~/.netrc, refreshed by the untracked
# `opread go` (see cheatsheet.md).
--ignore=install.*\.sh
--ignore=cheatsheet\.md
--ignore=check\.sh
--ignore=\.stowrc
--ignore=\.DS_Store
--ignore=zsh
--ignore=terminfo
--ignore=herdr
--ignore=macos
